# python3-sqlalchemy: the distro packages are 1.4 on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04;
# the module imports on 1.4 only with the compatibility shim in
# utils/models/sql.py (FlagGems-sglang#190).
# python3-torch is intentionally NOT declared. The distro 'python3-torch'
# is CPU-only and unsuitable for GPU workloads; users install matching
# torch via pip - see packaging/INSTALL.md.
# Triton is not a hard Depends either: the upstream python3-triton is too
# old (Ubuntu noble ships 2.0). python3-flagtree-nvidia is the
# distro-distributable option, so we Recommend it.
Recommends: python3-flagtree-nvidia
Suggests: python3-pytest
Description: FlagGems-sglang - Triton operator library for SGLang
 FlagGems-sglang is a high-performance operator library written in the
 Triton language for the SGLang inference engine. Operators are resolved
 at import time through a generic / vendor / architecture registrar, so
 one package serves every FlagOS backend.
 .
 Triton (provided here by python3-flagtree-nvidia or upstream
 python3-triton) and torch are required at runtime; without them the
 kernels cannot JIT-compile.
